Header-free mimic of libc++ std::tuple, cvise-reduced: the constructor
chain routes through __make_integer_seq / __type_pack_element
metafunctions and the instantiated member bodies are dropped ("no body
for callee tuple / get") even though the source defines them.  Gates
cpp11_libcxx_tuple and the test_libcxx variants of cpp11_tuple_basic,
cpp17_tuple_basic and cpp17_apply_basic.  clang++ accepts and runs
clean (clang-only builtins; g++ n/a).
Update 2026-07-28 (partial): four layers fixed (partial-spec pack
bindings persisted/replayed as #spec_template_packs; scalar _Idx and
empty-pack expansion in template-argument lists).  Remaining layer:
the member ctor template's pack-parameter deduction fails against the
pattern concretized by cross-scope short-name substitution
("found no match for symbol '__tuple_impl'"), the
cpp17_vector_emplace_nondefault_pair family.
Remaining-layer minimal reproducer: cpp11_two_pack_ctor_delegation.
Update 2026-07-30: the constructor-deduction layer is fixed
(cpp11_two_pack_ctor_delegation is CORE); the residual is again the
nil static_cast target in get -- the enclosing pre-bind that feeds
the __type_pack_element chain is CLANG-gated and this reproducer runs
in GCC mode (ungating regressed libstdc++ suites twice).
Update 2026-07-30 (round 4): in CLANG mode (--stdlib libc++) the
__tuple_impl ctor resolution regresses to the no-match layer even
though the pack-arity fixup computes correctly (probe: npacks=3
lead=2 size=1); the rebuilt instance is rejected by the second
disambiguation.  Mode-dependent resolution divergence; needs its own
session.
